# Governova — environment configuration
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is committed so the
# variable *names* are documented without any value ever being.
#
# EVERY VARIABLE HERE IS OPTIONAL. The deterministic engine — rules, probes, the
# Score, the Board Report, the System Bible, the CLI, the MCP server and the CI
# gate — runs with none of them set, offline, forever. That is a guarantee
# (`ADR-010` §5.1), not a default.
#
# S8.25 — `.env.example` is committed with all required variables documented;
#         `.env` itself is never committed.
# S3.20 — a real secret in a committed file is `AP-S3.20a`. Put values in `.env`.


# ─── Semantic tier (ADR-008) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The tier is INACTIVE unless configured, and says so when it is. There is no
# default endpoint: a default that lies converts an absent capability into a
# believed one, which is exactly how the tier reached nothing for two releases
# while every build stayed green.
#
# Any OpenAI-compatible or Anthropic-compatible endpoint works. A local model is
# the documented zero-cost route — no account, no cost, nothing leaves the machine.

# GOVERNOVA_LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# GOVERNOVA_LLM_MODEL=<a model served at that endpoint>
# GOVERNOVA_LLM_API_KEY=<any non-empty string; local servers ignore it>

# Wire protocol: `chat_completions` (default) or `messages`.
# GOVERNOVA_LLM_PROTOCOL=chat_completions

# Only for endpoints that require a dated API version (e.g. Azure).
# GOVERNOVA_LLM_API_VERSION=

# Seconds before a single review call is abandoned. Raising this to make a
# measurement complete would absorb a provider outage rather than report it.
# GOVERNOVA_LLM_TIMEOUT=30

# Ceiling on tokens per review response.
# GOVERNOVA_LLM_MAX_TOKENS=2048


# ─── Chat notifications ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Slack- or Teams-compatible incoming webhook for `governova notify`. Unset means
# the notifier does not run; it never fails a build either way.

# GOVERNOVA_WEBHOOK_URL=
# GOVERNOVA_WEBHOOK_TIMEOUT=10


# ─── Constitution source ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Path to a compiled `constitution.json`. Leave unset to use the copy bundled in
# the installed wheel.
#
# A source checkout bundles no constitution, so a command run against a FOREIGN
# directory finds nothing and exits before scanning. Set this when pointing the
# engine at a repository other than the one it was installed from.

# GOVERNOVA_CONSTITUTION=/path/to/compiled/constitution.json
